        "title": "We do not invent perfumes; we give sensory permanence to fleeting botanical memory.",
        "text": "<p>Each formulation emerges from an unhurried, six-month maturation period in charred French oak casks. Free of denatured synthetic alcohols, parabens, and aggressive stabilizers, our extraits remain raw, living compositions that adapt to the wearer's natural skin heat.</p><p>Collaborating between fifth-generation master noses in Grasse and heritage woodturners in Kyoto, Atelier Maison bridges French haute perfumery discipline with Japanese wabi-sabi restraint.</p>",
